  "summary": "Performance review of PR #470 (publish every validated review-round lane) found no blocking scaling defects. Review-stats stays windowed (max 50 PRs, concurrency 4) with fail-closed 100-record lane history. Round classification and provider-lane reuse are linear in marker count for realistic sizes. One advisory: the new multi-lane publish loop reloads issue comments and PR state once per lane for skip-match, and re-validates all sibling evidence files per lane (O(lanes × comments) provider work and O(lanes²) local validation), which is avoidable with a shared snapshot/evidence cache for a single gate invocation. Residual risk is wall-time on large PRs with many active lanes, not correctness.",
